# FluorineOS hardware support: firmware, microcode, and the userspace pieces
# each device class needs on Debian trixie.
#
# Every entry resolves to trixie or to trixie non-free-firmware. Nothing here
# comes from a third-party repository, and no driver is built from source, so
# the kernel stays the Debian kernel and upgrades stay ordinary APT upgrades.
#
# Packages are grouped by the subsystem that needs them, so a future change can
# be reviewed against one device class at a time. The reasoning for every group
# is in docs/HARDWARE.md.

# Kernel, GPU, and Wi-Fi firmware.
#
# firmware-linux is a metapackage over firmware-linux-free and
# firmware-linux-nonfree. In trixie that pulls only firmware-misc-nonfree and
# firmware-amd-graphics, so every other GPU and radio family is named here.
# Each of these packages backs a free in-kernel driver:
#   firmware-intel-graphics   i915/xe GuC, HuC, and DMC blobs. Gen12 and later
#                             need them for media decode and low-power states.
#   firmware-intel-sound      Intel SST audio DSP blobs.
#   firmware-sof-signed       Sound Open Firmware, the audio path on most Intel
#                             laptops from Ice Lake onward. Without it the
#                             internal speakers and microphone stay silent.
#   firmware-nvidia-graphics  nouveau/GSP blobs. Turing and newer cards cannot
#                             drive a display with nouveau without them.
#   firmware-brcm80211        Broadcom/Cypress Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.
#   firmware-mediatek         MediaTek MT76 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth, common on
#                             budget AMD laptops.
# firmware-qcom-soc is deliberately absent: it targets arm64 SoCs, and this
# image is amd64 only.
firmware-linux
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-nvidia-graphics
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek

# CPU microcode. The image is family-agnostic, so both blobs ship and the
# initramfs loads the one that matches the running CPU.
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

# Wireless. The regulatory database is what lets the stack pick legal channels
# and transmit power per country; without it a card comes up on the world
# domain. wpasupplicant is NetworkManager's WPA backend, and iw plus rfkill are
# the inspection tools flr-doctor and the troubleshooting docs rely on.
wireless-regdb
wpasupplicant
iw
rfkill

# Video decode. Mesa's VA driver covers AMD and the free NVIDIA path, and the
# Intel media driver covers Gen8 and newer; libva selects between them at
# runtime. vainfo is the check that reports which profiles are actually usable.
# i965-va-driver is not installed: it only matters for Intel graphics older
# than Gen8, and docs/HARDWARE.md says how to add it.
mesa-va-drivers
intel-media-va-driver
vainfo

# Audio and capture. pipewire-alsa gives ALSA-only applications a path into
# PipeWire instead of a dead device, and v4l-utils is the webcam control and
# query tool set.
pipewire-alsa
v4l-utils

# Storage. udisks2 is what Thunar's volume manager talks to for removable
# media, and exfatprogs formats the exFAT sticks that ship pre-formatted.
udisks2
exfatprogs

# Power. power-profiles-daemon backs flr-power and the Waybar power module, and
# upower feeds the battery module. brightness-udev installs the udev rules that
# let a session user change the panel and keyboard backlight without root.
# TLP is deliberately not installed: it and power-profiles-daemon manage the
# same platform profile and conflict.
power-profiles-daemon
upower
brightness-udev

# Hybrid graphics. D-Bus activated with no daemon at boot; it lets an
# application ask which GPUs exist before choosing one.
switcheroo-control

# Wayland-native Qt. Without the platform plugin Qt applications fall back to
# XWayland, which costs a full frame copy and ignores fractional scaling.
qt6-wayland

# Printing. CUPS is socket activated, and the PolicyKit helper is what the GTK
# printer dialogs authenticate through. avahi-daemon and libnss-mdns make
# network printers discoverable and resolve the .local names they advertise.
cups
cups-pk-helper
avahi-daemon
libnss-mdns

# Accessibility. Orca is Debian's screen reader; it reads GTK and Qt
# applications over AT-SPI, which the GTK stack already provides.
orca
